[% PROCESS util.tt -%]
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-md-12">
          <h1 class="section-title">Write for us</h1>

          <div class="hero mb-4">
            <p class="lead">
              Know something about Perl that deserves a book? We'd like to
              help you publish it.
            </p>
            <p>
              Perl School is an independent publisher specialising in books
              for the Perl community. We publish practical books by people
              who know their subjects, in ebook and paperback editions.
            </p>
            <div class="action-row">
              <a class="btn btn-primary"
                 href="mailto:hello@perlschool.com?subject=Book%20idea">
                Tell us your idea
              </a>
              <a class="btn btn-outline-primary" href="/books/">
                See our books
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h2 class="section-title">No subject is too niche</h2>

          <p>
            Large technical publishers need books with large potential
            audiences. We don't.
          </p>

          <p>
            Perl School was created partly because worthwhile Perl books were
            becoming difficult to publish through traditional technical
            publishers. Our lightweight publishing model means a book
            doesn't need to sell thousands of copies to be worth publishing.
          </p>

          <p>
            So don't worry that your idea is too specialised. If there's a
            group of Perl developers who would benefit from a good book about
            your subject, we're interested in hearing about it.
          </p>

          <h2 class="section-title">You write the book. We publish it.</h2>

          <p>
            You bring the expertise and the manuscript. We'll help with the
            rest.
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>Feedback and advice while you develop the book.</li>
            <li>Editing and proofreading.</li>
            <li>Production of ebook and print-ready editions.</li>
            <li>Publication and distribution through platforms such as
              Leanpub and Amazon.</li>
            <li>Print-on-demand paperback editions where appropriate.</li>
            <li>Ongoing updates when your book needs them.</li>
          </ul>

          <p>
            Our aim is to let you concentrate on explaining your subject
            rather than learning the mechanics of publishing.
          </p>

          <h2 class="section-title">The book is ready when it's ready</h2>

          <p>
            Most Perl School authors have jobs, open-source projects,
            families and other demands on their time. Life happens.
          </p>

          <p>
            We won't give you an arbitrary publication date and then pressure
            you to meet it. We'll agree how we want to work together and help
            you keep making progress, but we'll publish the book when we're
            both happy that it's ready.
          </p>

          <h2 class="section-title">Authors get 85%</h2>

          <p>
            Our low-overhead publishing model also lets us offer unusually
            simple economics.
          </p>

          <p>
            <strong>
              You receive 85% of the money Perl School receives from sales
              of your book. Perl School keeps 15%.
            </strong>
          </p>

          <p>
            That's 85% of the money paid to us by retailers and publishing
            platforms, not a small royalty calculated after a traditional
            publisher has taken its share.
          </p>

          <p>
            We'll explain exactly how the arrangement works before you commit
            to anything.
          </p>

          <h2 class="section-title">What are we looking for?</h2>

          <p>
            Books about Perl.
          </p>

          <p>
            That might be a guide to a particular module or framework, a book
            about a specialist technique, an introduction to an area of Perl
            development, or a new edition of an older book whose rights have
            returned to its author.
          </p>

          <p>
            We like practical experience, clear explanations and examples
            that help readers get things done. Beyond that, we're deliberately
            open-minded.
          </p>

          <h2 class="section-title">Have an idea?</h2>

          <p>
            You don't need a finished manuscript or a formal book proposal.
            Tell us what you'd like to write, who you think would read it,
            and why you're the right person to write it.
          </p>

          <p>
            If you already have an outline, sample chapter, conference talk,
            blog post or repository that helps explain the idea, send that
            too. But don't create one just for us before we've talked.
          </p>

          <p>
            Email
            <a href="mailto:hello@perlschool.com?subject=Book%20idea">hello@perlschool.com</a>
            or just use the button below to start the conversation.
          </p>

          <div class="action-row">
            <a class="btn btn-primary"
               href="mailto:hello@perlschool.com?subject=Book%20idea">
              Tell us your idea
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
